    fix: teach absorb --window error the accepted trail shape. Addresses LORE-053.
    
    The absorb --window error quoted internal tooling state (the logsey
    export contract status) and used one identical message for two unrelated
    failure modes. Now:
    - no export marker at all -> empty/unclaimed input: exit 0 with the
      existing 'no classifiable evidence blocks' message (unchanged parse
      behavior, message now asserted by a subprocess-level test);
    - marker present but no fenced block -> exit 2 with a teaching error
      naming the accepted shape plus one example timestamp line;
    - marker + fenced block but no parseable lines -> exit 2 with the
      distinguishable teaching error.
    LOGSEY_EXPORT_SHAPE_HINT is the user-facing constant; the honest
    contract status stays in docstrings/tests only.
    510 -> 514 tests (count guard + living docs synced).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
